            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis and pharmacological evaluation of novel antinociceptive N-substituted-phenylimidazolyl-4-acylhydrazone derivatives.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>999-1007</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper describes recent results of design, synthesis and pharmacological evaluation of new N-heterocyclic functionalized N-acylhydrazone compounds (NAH), belonging to the N-substituted-phenylimidazolyl-4-acylhydrazone class (3a-o). These compounds were planned by applying the molecular hybridization strategy to propose the structural modifications on the previously described functionalized 2-methyl-imidazolyl-3-acylhydrazone class (2), which presented an important analgesic profile. This new series (3) was synthesized in order to investigate the possible pharmacophoric contribution of the N-heteroaromatic ring and N-acylhydrazone moieties to the analgesic activity. Compounds 3g and 3n are the most potent analgesic agents from this series, at the screening dose of 100 mg/kg p.o. and compounds 3e, 3j and 3o presented the best antiinflammatory properties at the same screening concentration.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
